# PHASE ORCHESTRATION

> **Purpose:** Drive the 6-phase forensic documentation workflow with per-section RGV loops and progressive file writing.
> **Enforcement:** See `@03_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`

---

## WORKFLOW STATE MACHINE

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> P0: Start
    P0 --> P1: Inventory complete
    P1 --> P2: Orchestrations documented
    P2 --> P3: Schemas & Maps documented
    P3 --> P4: Pipelines, Ports & Helpers documented
    P4 --> P5: Replication-readiness assessed
    P5 --> [*]: Zero data loss certified
```

---

## DELIBERATION TRIGGER

Before EVERY phase and EVERY section, produce a `<thinking>` block. Slow down: an omission becomes a defect in the rebuilt MuleSoft integration. Think before you extract.

```
<thinking>
1. Inputs received: [files/elements in scope for this section]
2. Decisions: [what to extract, where logic lives (.btm vs .xsl), how to structure]
3. Evidence from source: [cite file + element/OID/LinkID]
4. Risks/gaps: [missing assembly? UTF-16? external schema? encrypted value?]
5. Confidence: HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW [justify]
6. Error premortem: [most likely way this section is wrong → how I prevent it]
</thinking>
```

---

## PER-PHASE WRITE CONTRACT (Progressive Documentation v2)

Skeleton-first, then write one bounded section group per phase. Never regenerate the whole file to edit one section — use targeted edits.

| Phase | Writes To (file) | Section / Marker | Mode |
|-------|------------------|------------------|------|
| 0 | main doc + `artifact-inventory.md` | `<!-- SECTION:1 -->`, `<!-- SECTION:2 -->` | Create skeleton (all 7 markers) + fill 1-2 |
| 1 | main doc + `orchestration-flows.md` | `<!-- SECTION:3 -->` | Append per-orchestration |
| 2 | main doc + `schema-structures.md` + `map-mappings.md` | `<!-- SECTION:4 -->` | Append per-schema / per-map |
| 3 | main doc + `pipeline-helper-reference.md` | `<!-- SECTION:5 -->` | Append per-pipeline / per-helper |
| 4 | main doc + `replication-gap-report.md` | `<!-- SECTION:6 -->` | Append mapping + gaps |
| 5 | main doc + `verification-checklist.md` | `<!-- SECTION:7 -->` | **Consolidate & Polish** (reconcile, do NOT regenerate prior sections) |

> **Phase 0 Step 1 = create the main-doc skeleton** with named placeholders for all 7 sections, then fill Sections 1-2.

---

## RGV (READ-GENERATE-VERIFY) PATTERN

Apply per section in Phases 1-4. Full definition (DRY) in `@02_Guidance.mdc §1`.

```
1. RE-READ   — Fresh Read on ALL relevant artifact files for this section
2. INVENTORY — Count target elements, COMMIT to N (e.g., "Process_X has 14 shapes")
3. GENERATE  — Produce content with exactly N items
4. VERIFY    — Count generated, compare to N → "Processed N/N"
5. FIX       — If N≠generated, RE-READ, find missing, fix before checkpoint
6. CHECKPOINT— Emit count-verified micro-checkpoint, write to file, proceed
```

> If counts don't match, do NOT proceed. Fix first.

---

## FORENSIC INPUT PROCESSING (Heavy input — REQUIRED)

BizTalk exports are large and heterogeneous. Counter Attention Drift / Positional Bias / Error Cascade:

1. **INVENTORY (mind map)** — In Phase 0 build a structural index of every artifact (type, name, path, references). This is the verification baseline.
2. **SECTION-BY-SECTION** — Process each orchestration/schema/map/pipeline/helper in isolation with its own RGV.
3. **POSITIONAL BIAS SCAN** — For long `.odx`/`.xsl` files, re-read the middle 30%-70% to catch shapes/links missed on first pass.
4. **COMPLETENESS VERIFICATION** — Compare processed counts against the Phase 0 mind map baseline.
5. **CROSS-ARTIFACT COHERENCE** — Verify a map referenced by an orchestration exists; a schema referenced by a map exists; flag any dangling reference as 🔴 GAP.

