## PHASE SPECIFICATIONS

### PHASE 0 — Discovery & Inventory
- **Read:** `.sln`/`.btproj` (project structure + assembly refs), then enumerate all `.odx`/`.btm`/`.xsl`/`.xsd`/`.btp`/`.cs`.
- **Do:** classify + count each artifact type; build assembly-reference graph; identify referenced-but-absent assemblies/schemas; create main-doc skeleton (7 markers); fill Sections 1-2.
- **Write:** main doc Sections 1-2, `artifact-inventory.md`.
- **Checkpoint:** `✅ Phase 0: {app} — {X} orchestrations, {Y} maps, {Z} schemas, {P} pipelines, {H} helpers inventoried`.

### PHASE 1 — Orchestration Documentation
- **Per `.odx` (RGV):** count shapes; document each shape (Receive/Send/Construct/Transform/Decision/Loop/Scope/Call/Assignment/Parallel), ports, message + variable declarations, correlations, DNF filter predicates, complete inline expression code; build a Mermaid flow per orchestration.
- **Write:** main doc Section 3, `orchestration-flows.md`.
- **Checkpoint per orchestration:** `✅ 1.k: {OrchName} — {n}/{n} shapes`.

### PHASE 2 — Schema & Map Documentation
- **Per `.xsd` (RGV):** document field tree (element/attribute, type, occurrence, namespace), root + target-namespace. Handle UTF-16/BOM.
- **Per map (RGV):** read the paired `.xsl` for transform logic AND the `.btm` for functoid graph/constants; document EVERY link (source XPath → target XPath + functoid/logic). Note `CustomXSLT` when used.
- **Write:** main doc Section 4, `schema-structures.md`, `map-mappings.md`.
- **Checkpoint per map:** `✅ 2.k: {MapName} — {n}/{n} links`.

### PHASE 3 — Pipeline, Port & Helper Documentation
- **Per `.btp` (RGV):** stages → components.
- **Per `.cs` helper (RGV):** class, public method signatures, summarized logic + complete code; list orchestration call-sites. If a referenced helper has NO source, document the call-site/signature and flag 🔴 GAP.
- **Write:** main doc Section 5, `pipeline-helper-reference.md`.
- **Checkpoint:** `✅ Phase 3: {P}/{P} pipelines, {H}/{H} helpers documented`.

### PHASE 4 — Replication-Readiness & Gap Assessment
- **Do:** build the BizTalk-construct → MuleSoft-equivalent table; assign a verdict per artifact (🟢 replicable / 🟡 ambiguous / 🔴 blocked); list every replication gap with reason + recommended MuleSoft action.
- **Write:** main doc Section 6, `replication-gap-report.md`.
- **Checkpoint:** `✅ Phase 4: {G} replication gaps identified; verdicts assigned to {A}/{A} artifacts`.

### PHASE 5 — Validation & Certification
- **Do:** file-by-file reconciliation (elements found vs documented) using the Phase 0 mind map; aggregate coverage; emit certification. **Consolidate & Polish — do NOT regenerate prior sections.**
- **Write:** main doc Section 7, `verification-checklist.md`.
- **Checkpoint:** certification block (see `@00_Template_Configuration.mdc`).

---

## CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION

| Confidence | When | Action |
|------------|------|--------|
| **HIGH** | Source artifact present + fully readable | Document directly with citations |
| **MEDIUM** | Logic inferable but partial (e.g., functoid graph dense, `.xsl` clarifies) | Document + flag ⚠️ ASSUMPTION, cross-check both files |
| **LOW** | Referenced artifact absent / encrypted / external | **Do NOT guess** — document call-site + flag 🔴 GAP |

